pt;\">05</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 706px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 28px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 28.1437%; text-align: center; height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 71.8563%; text-align: center; height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Eligibility Criteria</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 161px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 28.1437%; text-align: center; height: 161px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Manager</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 71.8563%; height: 161px;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have either a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"244\" data-start=\"61\">Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Commerce or a Bachelor\u2019s Degree with Economics, Mathematics, or Statistics with at least 55% marks along with basic computer knowledge (O Level or equivalent)</strong>,\u00a0<strong data-end=\"252\" data-start=\"246\">or</strong>\u00a0a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"334\" data-start=\"255\">B.Tech / B.E. in Computer Science or IT, BCA, or MCA with minimum 55% marks</strong>,\u00a0<strong data-end=\"342\" data-start=\"336\">or</strong>\u00a0a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"462\" data-start=\"345\">BBA / MBA in Banking, Finance, or HR or a full-time PGDM in Banking, Finance, or HR from a recognized institution</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 161px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 28.1437%; text-align: center; height: 161px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Junior Manager</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 71.8563%; height: 161px;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have either a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"244\" data-start=\"61\">Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Commerce or a Bachelor\u2019s Degree with Economics, Mathematics, or Statistics with at least 55% marks along with basic computer knowledge (O Level or equivalent)</strong>,\u00a0<strong data-end=\"252\" data-start=\"246\">or</strong>\u00a0a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"316\" data-start=\"255\">B.Tech / B.E. (CS/IT), BCA, or MCA with minimum 55% marks</strong>,\u00a0<strong data-end=\"324\" data-start=\"318\">or</strong>\u00a0a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"444\" data-start=\"327\">BBA / MBA in Banking, Finance, or HR or a full-time PGDM in Banking, Finance, or HR from a recognized institution</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 110px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 28.1437%; text-align: center; height: 110px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Assistant/ Cashier (Banking Assistant/Clerical Staff)</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 71.8563%; height: 110px;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"173\" data-start=\"54\">Bachelor\u2019s Degree with at least 55% marks from any recognized university or institution established by law in India</strong>, along with a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"227\" data-start=\"188\">minimum CCC certificate in computer</strong>, which is mandatory.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 136px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 28.1437%; text-align: center; height: 136px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Assistant/Typist\u00a0</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 71.8563%; height: 136px;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"145\" data-start=\"54\">Graduation degree from a recognized university or institute established by law in India</strong>, along with\u00a0<strong data-end=\"241\" data-start=\"158\">typing speed of 30 words per minute in Hindi and 40 words per minute in English</strong>. Additionally, a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"311\" data-start=\"259\">minimum CCC certificate in computer is mandatory</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 110px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 28.1437%; text-align: center; height: 110px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Assistant Engineer (Civil)</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 71.8563%; height: 110px;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"229\" data-start=\"54\">Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Civil Engineering from a recognized university or institution established by law in India, or an equivalent qualification recognized by the Government</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"background-color: #000080; color: #ffffff; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>\u00a0How To Check &amp; Download UPCISB UP Co-operative Bank Various Post Exam Date 2026\u00a0</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<ul>\n<li data-end=\"124\" data-section-id=\"cx84fe\" data-start=\"88\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Visit the official UPCISB website.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"245\" data-section-id=\"lp3f23\" data-start=\"125\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">On the homepage, click on the <strong data-end=\"211\" data-start=\"157\">\u201cUP Co-operative Bank Various Post Exam Date 2026\u201d</strong> or <strong data-end=\"239\" data-start=\"215\">Latest Notifications</strong> link.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"282\" data-section-id=\"16mhxxi\" data-start=\"246\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Open the <strong data-end=\"277\" data-start=\"257\">Exam Date Notice</strong> PDF.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"377\" data-section-id=\"tec5z2\" data-start=\"283\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Check the <strong data-end=\"366\" data-start=\"295\">exam date, exam schedule, shift timings, and important instructions</strong> carefully.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"433\" data-section-id=\"iew877\" data-start=\"378\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Verify all the details mentioned in the notification.</span></li>\n<li dat